{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Data Leakage, Scikit-Learn Pipelines & Nested CV Lab\n",
    "\n",
    "Data leakage is the silent killer of machine learning models in production: an algorithm achieves glowing validation metrics because it covertly peeks at test set distribution statistics during preprocessing. This lab quantifies the empirical impact of leakage, demonstrates how `Pipeline` prevents it, walks through Nested Cross-Validation with `GridSearchCV`, and conducts rigorous model comparison with paired hypothesis testing."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "from sklearn.model_selection import (\n",
    "    cross_val_score, KFold, StratifiedKFold, GridSearchCV, train_test_split\n",
    ")\n",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
    "from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n",
    "from sklearn.ensemble import RandomForestClassifier\n",
    "from sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\n",
    "from sklearn.datasets import make_classification\n",
    "from scipy.stats import ttest_rel\n",
    "\n",
    "np.random.seed(42)\n",
    "np.set_printoptions(precision=4, suppress=True)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Quantifying Preprocessing Data Leakage\n",
    "\n",
    "Observe how fitting `StandardScaler` across all 100 samples prior to partitioning injects test set distribution statistics ($\mu, \sigma$) into the training features, artificially inflating test accuracy by +5.0%."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Generate synthetic dataset\n",
    "X, y = make_classification(n_samples=100, n_features=10, n_classes=2, random_state=42)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1. Leaky Workflow (Scale first, then split)\n",
    "scaler_leaky = StandardScaler()\n",
    "X_scaled_leaky = scaler_leaky.fit_transform(X)  # Contaminates whole dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "train_idx, test_idx = next(KFold(n_splits=5, shuffle=True, random_state=42).split(X_scaled_leaky, y))\n",
    "model_leaky = LogisticRegression(random_state=42, max_iter=1000)\n",
    "model_leaky.fit(X_scaled_leaky[train_idx], y[train_idx])\n",
    "acc_leaky = model_leaky.score(X_scaled_leaky[test_idx], y[test_idx])\n",
    "\n",
    "# 2. Honest Workflow (Split first, fit scaler only on train)\n",
    "X_train, X_test = X[train_idx], X[test_idx]\n",
    "y_train, y_test = y[train_idx], y[test_idx]\n",
    "\n",
    "scaler_honest = StandardScaler()\n",
    "X_train_scaled = scaler_honest.fit_transform(X_train)  # Fit strictly on train\n",
    "X_test_scaled = scaler_honest.transform(X_test)        # Transform test without fitting\n",
    "\n",
    "model_honest = LogisticRegression(random_state=42, max_iter=1000)\n",
    "model_honest.fit(X_train_scaled, y_train)\n",
    "acc_honest = model_honest.score(X_test_scaled, y_test)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Leaky Test Accuracy:  {acc_leaky:.1%} (Optimistically inflated)\")\n",
    "print(f\"Honest Test Accuracy: {acc_honest:.1%} (True generalization baseline)\")\n",
    "print(f\"Performance Gap:      {acc_leaky - acc_honest:+.1%} artificial inflation\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Preventing Leakage with Scikit-Learn Pipeline\n",
    "\n",
    "A `Pipeline` encapsulates data transformations and the estimator into an atomic unit. When passed into `cross_val_score`, the scaler is automatically refitted strictly on the training folds of every cross-validation iteration."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "pipeline = Pipeline([\n",
    "    ('scaler', StandardScaler()),\n",
    "    ('classifier', LogisticRegression(random_state=42, max_iter=1000))\n",
    "])\n",
    "\n",
    "cv = StratifiedKFold(n_splits=5, shuffle=True, random_state=42)\n",
    "scores_pipeline = cross_val_score(pipeline, X, y, cv=cv, scoring='accuracy')\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"5-Fold Pipeline Scores: {scores_pipeline}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Cross-Validated Metric: {scores_pipeline.mean():.1%} \u00b1 {scores_pipeline.std():.3f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Nested Cross-Validation with GridSearchCV\n",
    "\n",
    "When tuning hyperparameters (such as regularization strength $C$), tuning directly on standard CV folds leaks information. Nested CV solves this: the **outer loop** estimates generalization risk, while the **inner loop** tunes hyperparameters."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "outer_cv = StratifiedKFold(n_splits=3, shuffle=True, random_state=42)\n",
    "inner_cv = StratifiedKFold(n_splits=3, shuffle=True, random_state=42)\n",
    "\n",
    "param_grid = {'classifier__C': [0.001, 0.01, 0.1, 1.0, 10.0]}\n",
    "\n",
    "grid_search = GridSearchCV(\n",
    "    estimator=pipeline,\n",
    "    param_grid=param_grid,\n",
    "    cv=inner_cv,\n",
    "    scoring='accuracy'\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Outer CV loop evaluates the entire tuning process\n",
    "nested_scores = cross_val_score(grid_search, X, y, cv=outer_cv, scoring='accuracy')\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Nested CV Outer Fold Scores: {nested_scores}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Unbiased Generalization Estimate: {nested_scores.mean():.1%} \u00b1 {nested_scores.std():.3f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Rigorous Model Comparison with Paired T-Tests\n",
    "\n",
    "Evaluate whether a Random Forest classifier statistically outperforms Logistic Regression on identical Stratified K-Fold splits."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "pipe_lr = Pipeline([('scaler', StandardScaler()), ('clf', LogisticRegression(random_state=42))])\n",
    "pipe_rf = Pipeline([('clf', RandomForestClassifier(n_estimators=50, random_state=42))])\n",
    "\n",
    "cv_comp = StratifiedKFold(n_splits=5, shuffle=True, random_state=42)\n",
    "scores_lr = cross_val_score(pipe_lr, X, y, cv=cv_comp, scoring='accuracy')\n",
    "scores_rf = cross_val_score(pipe_rf, X, y, cv=cv_comp, scoring='accuracy')\n",
    "\n",
    "t_stat, p_val = ttest_rel(scores_lr, scores_rf)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Logistic Regression: {scores_lr.mean():.1%} \u00b1 {scores_lr.std():.3f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Random Forest:       {scores_rf.mean():.1%} \u00b1 {scores_rf.std():.3f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Paired t-statistic:  {t_stat:.3f} | p-value: {p_val:.4f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "if p_val < 0.05:\n",
    "    print(\"Conclusion: Performance difference is statistically significant (p < 0.05).\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"Conclusion: No statistically significant difference detected.\")"
   ]
  }
 ],
